@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# FrozenMessagesRail
+
+An opt-in exact-message, single-response Rail for a fresh, tool-free openJiuwen ReActAgent. This extension is independently exercised on openjiuwen 0.1.16.post20; compatibility with other SDK revisions is not implied.
+
+The constructor accepts a nonempty list of dictionaries containing exactly role and string content. Supported roles are system, user and assistant. It defensively copies the prepared messages, preserves their ordering and checks the final model transport immediately before delegation. Tools, streaming, a second model invocation or changed messages are refused. The optional synchronous callback receives the SDK response and the actual transport-associated role/content messages before post-response checks, so callers can durably retain billable evidence.
+
+```python
+from jiuwenswarm.agents.harness.common.rails.frozen_messages_rail import FrozenMessagesRail
+
+messages = [
+    {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Use supplied evidence only.'},
+    {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Prepared evidence and question'},
+]
+rail = FrozenMessagesRail(messages, on_response=persist_response)
+# Configure a new ReActAgent with max_iterations=1, no tools and no extra prompts.
+await agent.register_rail(rail)
+await agent.invoke({'query': messages[-1]['content'], 'conversation_id': 'fresh-id'})
+```
+
+The tested SDK rebuilds its context window after before_model_call. This Rail therefore delegates context behavior through a temporary exact-window proxy and guards the final model invoke, rather than assuming that replacing the preliminary message list is enough. It restores the original context on response or model exception. These are version-sensitive integration points; the tests patch the actual SDK transport and prove that a reflection sequence (system/user/assistant/user) arrives unchanged and exactly once.
+
+For the research runtime, research/agent_invocation.py converts response usage metadata to the durable gateway callback and verifies the response count and actual inputs again. The Rail itself does not infer prices, classify exceptions as free, resolve source conflicts, access gold labels, retry transports or provide general multi-turn memory. Always use a new agent/Rail per invocation. An unknown or missing usage record must remain unknown.
+
+This local contribution is provided as source and patch. No upstream PR, merge or review acceptance is claimed.
